A||||6||Eric||Paint Stripper
Z||000000||Eric||07-24-99||02:40 PM||||What kind of paint stripper should I use on my bumpers?  They look like rubber, but I'm not sure about it, so I don't want to buy a rubber stripper until I know for sure.
Z||000001||PaUL||07-24-99||03:37 PM||||I can tell you exactly what its made of: Reaction injection molded urethane. Also refered to as RIM plastic.
Z||000002||Phil||07-24-99||06:27 PM||||There is a special stripper that  takes aftermarket paint off of factory finish. If you leave it on for a while it will eventually remove bumper paint. I got it at my local automotive paint supplier $10 a spray can. If you are going to repaint you don't have to remove the factory finish. If all else fails sandpaper works
Z||000003||Eric||07-24-99||07:33 PM||||I know the rear bumper wasn't original because there was overspray on the license plate light.
Z||000004||theogre||07-24-99||09:13 PM||||use extream care with ALL chem strips on Fiero. You can do major damage.<p>you don't need to stip to repaint. You do need to make sure there is no loose paint. Flakes, chips, etc, must all be removed.<p>Use 400-600 Aluminum Oxide paper for final sanding and sand the entire surface. This breaks paint glaze, and removes waxes, etc.
Z||000005||Punkndrublic||07-25-99||05:11 PM||||I just a bought a spoiler from the reckers, except its red and my car is silver, i want to remove all the paint but im afraid that whatever chemicals i use might reck the specail plastic fiberglass stuff its made out of. Any sugguestions as to what to use???
Z||000006||Racer 1||07-26-99||12:16 PM||||Acrylic lacquer thinner is your ticket.Buy the cheapest stuff.It makes the paint come off easily just by wiping it off with a towel.But when you paint your bumper dont use spay can junk.
